### Sign in as a citizen first (see 02-auth.http) so {{token}} is set, and pick an issue id
@issueId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Before reporting: is this already reported nearby?
GET {{host}}/api/v1/issues/similar?latitude=18.5204&longitude=73.8567&category=POTHOLE&title=pothole near bus stop

### Possible duplicates of an existing issue
GET {{host}}/api/v1/issues/{{issueId}}/similar

### Agree that the problem exists (citizens only, not on your own report; safe to repeat)
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/issues/{{issueId}}/vote
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "value": "AGREE" }

### Vote counts (public)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/issues/{{issueId}}/votes

### Comment (anyone signed in; at most 3 per person per issue)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/issues/{{issueId}}/comments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "body": "Same problem outside our building." }

### Comments (public, oldest first)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/issues/{{issueId}}/comments

### My notifications, newest first
GET {{host}}/api/v1/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
GET {{host}}/api/v1/notifications/unread-count
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
POST {{host}}/api/v1/notifications/read-all
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Live stream: get a one-time ticket, then open the streamUrl in a browser EventSource
POST {{host}}/api/v1/notifications/stream-ticket
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

> {% client.global.set("streamUrl", response.body.streamUrl); %}

### Opens the stream (IntelliJ shows events as they arrive; stop the request to close it)
GET {{host}}{{streamUrl}}
Accept: text/event-stream
